CommitDate: Thu Sep 10 08:39:13 2026 +0900

    Add optional RasterIX support for Nexys Video
    
    Expose a configurable external APB port and connect the unmodified
    upstream RasterIX submodule through command/response clock-crossing
    FIFOs. Share DDR3 with Wally and the DVI framebuffer using buffered
    GPU bursts and acknowledged framebuffer swaps.
    
    Add the nexysvideo-rasterix build target, video clocks and constraints,
    a reserved-memory device tree, and a Linux OpenGL example using the
    upstream library. Keep the external APB configuration independent of
    the board-specific renderer selection.
    
    Validated the qualified bitstream with three Linux boot cycles,
    full-frame readbacks, device-data transfers, CoreMark, a 4 MiB memory
    test, 3600 rendered frames, and a 39.95-second HDMI recording.
    HDMI capture reacquisition after FPGA reconfiguration was intermittent
    in the test setup; reinitializing the capture source restored it.

